    {
      "id": "iWqUcmQ-lqfhPhthB9GPK",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3041.417968749999,
      "y": 2912.5641741071427,
      "width": 1439.8587646484375,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aM",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1371225594,
      "version": 705,
      "versionNonce": 1751397670,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1777159318183,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Trade off of human oversight\n\n- Latency: Human review steps can introduce significant delays, impacting real-time agent responsiveness\n\n- Cost: Involving human labor, expecially for frequent or complex reviews, can be expensive\n\n- Scalability: May become bottlenecks as the volume of agent actions or interactoins increases, making it difficult for humans to keep pace.\n\n- Fatigue: Over-escalation of routing or non-critical issues can lead to human reviewers becoming fatigued or desensitized, potentially missing truly \n    important interventions. Balancing these factors is key to designing effective and sustainable human oversight into agentic systems.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Trade off of human oversight\n\n- Latency: Human review steps can introduce significant delays, impacting real-time agent responsiveness\n\n- Cost: Involving human labor, expecially for frequent or complex reviews, can be expensive\n\n- Scalability: May become bottlenecks as the volume of agent actions or interactoins increases, making it difficult for humans to keep pace.\n\n- Fatigue: Over-escalation of routing or non-critical issues can lead to human reviewers becoming fatigued or desensitized, potentially missing truly \n    important interventions. Balancing these factors is key to designing effective and sustainable human oversight into agentic systems.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "_30SnoMl-VFqZWm94V4U4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1942.9670758928569,
      "y": 3676.4369419642844,
      "width": 2165.71826171875,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aN",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1963291174,
      "version": 1237,
      "versionNonce": 62701434,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1777162296268,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "High Inference latency:\n\nHigh latency -> higher operational costs, more powerful or numerous computing resources are needed to compensate.\n\n\n- Judicious model selection: small model for simple task and larfer for complex reasioning, planning, or creative generation.\n\n- Model Optimization: Techniques like quantization, pruning, and knowledge distillation to reduce the model's size and computational requiremetns without significant loss of accuracy. (Lighter and faster for deployment)\n\n- Caching mechanisms: cache the response for frequently requested or deterministic outputs\n\n- Parallelizaton of operations: perform multiple LLM calls or tool invocations concurrently rather than sequentially.\n\n- Asynchronous processing: don't require immediate user response (backend data processing, report generation) system to continue processing other requests without waiting for long-running tasks to complete\n\n- Hardware acceleration and deployment strategy: Leverage specialized hardware (GPUs, TPUs) and optimize deployment for low-latency inference. Consider edge computing if responsiveness to localized inputs is paramount.\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "High Inference latency:\n\nHigh latency -> higher operational costs, more powerful or numerous computing resources are needed to compensate.\n\n\n- Judicious model selection: small model for simple task and larfer for complex reasioning, planning, or creative generation.\n\n- Model Optimization: Techniques like quantization, pruning, and knowledge distillation to reduce the model's size and computational requiremetns without significant loss of accuracy. (Lighter and faster for deployment)\n\n- Caching mechanisms: cache the response for frequently requested or deterministic outputs\n\n- Parallelizaton of operations: perform multiple LLM calls or tool invocations concurrently rather than sequentially.\n\n- Asynchronous processing: don't require immediate user response (backend data processing, report generation) system to continue processing other requests without waiting for long-running tasks to complete\n\n- Hardware acceleration and deployment strategy: Leverage specialized hardware (GPUs, TPUs) and optimize deployment for low-latency inference. Consider edge computing if responsiveness to localized inputs is paramount.\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "E9HJKq0PENpshdOL80gQI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1953.5608258928569,
      "y": 4204.421316964284,
      "width": 625.6395874023438,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aP",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1402049894,
      "version": 233,
      "versionNonce": 2027267942,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1777162369663,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Security and privacy vulnerabilities\n\n- Prompt injection (manipulating prompts to bypass safety)\n- Jailbreaking (coaxing the LLM into generating harmful content)\n- Unintentional data leakage (exposing sensitive user data)\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Security and privacy vulnerabilities\n\n- Prompt injection (manipulating prompts to bypass safety)\n- Jailbreaking (coaxing the LLM into generating harmful content)\n- Unintentional data leakage (exposing sensitive user data)\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
